<worksheet >
    <title>DC-2 The Chain Rule</title>
  <introduction>
    <p>To earn an M on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete all three parts. 
      To earn a P on this outcome, you will need to correctly complete two parts with progress on the third.</p>
  </introduction>  
  <page>
    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <introduction><p>Let <m>f(x,y)=x^3\sin(y)</m> where <m>x(u,v)=u^2-v</m> and <m>y(u,v)=3u+v^2</m>.</p></introduction>
        <task><statement><p>Find <m>\frac{\partial f}{\partial u}</m>.</p></statement></task>
        <task><statement><p>Find <m>\frac{\partial f}{\partial v}</m>.</p></statement></task>
        <task><statement><p>If <m>u(t)=t^2+1</m> and <m>v(t)=2t</m>, find <m>\frac{df}{dt}</m>.</p></statement></task>
    </exercise>
  </page>
</worksheet>